.\" Manual page for oc-plugin-updater.
.TH OC-PLUGIN-UPDATER 1 "October 2026" "oc-plugin-updater 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
oc-plugin-updater \- cross-platform updater for OpenCode npm plugins
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B oc-plugin-updater
.RI [ options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Reads the plugin list from OpenCode's config (v1
.I plugin
and v2
.IR plugins ,
across
.IR opencode.jsonc ", " opencode.json " and " tui.json(c) ),
resolves target versions from the npm registry, resets OpenCode's plugin
package cache (v1
.I packages
and v2
.I npm
layouts), and reinstalls with pnpm or npm. Config files are never written.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-\-list
Print the full version catalogue for each plugin and exit.
.TP
.BR \-\-pick
Choose target versions interactively (arrows/j/k, / filter, Space select,
Enter confirm, Esc cancel; requires a TTY).
.TP
.BR "\-\-set " \fIname@version\fR
Target an exact version/tag for a plugin (repeatable).
.TP
.BR "\-\-only " \fIname\fR
Process only the named plugin (repeatable).
.TP
.BR \-\-notify
Check-only mode: report available updates and exit 4 when any exist,
0 otherwise. Suitable for schedulers (cron, launchd, Task Scheduler).
.TP
.BR \-\-json
Machine-readable output; supports
.BR \-\-list ", " \-\-notify " and " \-\-dry-run .
.TP
.BR \-\-git\-pull
Run
.B git pull \-\-ff\-only
in the config directory before reading it.
.TP
.BR "\-\-completions " \fIshell\fR
Print a completion script for
.IR bash ", " zsh " or " pwsh .
.TP
.BR \-\-clean
Remove cached wrappers whose plugin is no longer in any config.
.TP
.BR "\-\-remove " \fIname\fR
Delete a plugin's cached wrappers (config stays untouched).
.TP
.BR \-\-backup
Snapshot wrappers before replacing them; a failed install auto-restores.
.TP
.BR \-\-rollback
Restore the most recent backup of each updated wrapper.
.TP
.BR \-\-doctor
Report paths, config generation, cache layout, binaries, locks, tools.
.TP
.BR "\-\-registry " \fIurl\fR
Use a custom npm registry (mirror) for lookups and installs.
.TP
.BR \-\-dry\-run
Show what would change; touch nothing.
.TP
.BR \-\-yes ", " \-y
Non-interactive: accept defaults, skip prompts.
.TP
.BR \-\-all
Uncap catalogue lists.
.TP
.BR "\-\-pm " \fIpnpm|npm\fR
Force a package manager.
.TP
.BR "\-\-config\-dir " \fIdir\fR ", " "\-\-cache\-dir " \fIdir\fR
Override path detection.
.TP
.BR \-\-kill\-blockers
Kill processes holding package files locked.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success (or everything up to date).
.TP
.B 1
Install/verify failure.
.TP
.B 2
Usage or path error.
.TP
.B 3
Files locked by running processes.
.TP
.B 4
Updates available (only from
.BR \-\-notify ).
.SH LIBRARY
.B import { updatePlugins, checkUpdates } from 'oc-plugin-updater'
\-\- both accept
.IR configDir ", " cacheDir ", " pm ", " registry ", " yes ", " dryRun ", " only ", " set
and resolve with the CLI exit code.
